  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun/Jul) to 1,180-1,260/month (Aug/Sep) (E-05), and the 1,240 disputed bills built on ESTIMATED reads (of 3,025 disputed bills total, E-01) trace to billing-import rule BV-17 (deployed 2026-08-01, unit_scaling=none, E-14) rejecting valid AMI reads from firmware-v4.2 meters as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION (1,184 such reads, E-12) because v4.2 reports consumption in '0.1 m3' units that appear ~10x inflated against m3-based history (E-13), forcing those accounts onto disputed estimated bills. This confirmed BV-17/firmware-unit mechanism explains the ESTIMATED-read dispute population but does not yet account for the 1,785 ACTUAL-read disputed bills that form the stated majority (59%, E-01)."
 },
